  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">White Nile WASH response to South Sudanese host community</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide access to water, sanitation and health services for 74000 people - both host community and South Sudan refugees - in 6 camps in White Nile state. CAFOD&#x2019;s national partner SIDO will build on the activities of other agencies in the region.

To improve access to safe water, SIDO will construct 12 water distribution points in six camps and a water supply pipeline in one camp, with water supply systems for 4 schools..

To improve sanitation, SIDO will construct communal latrines; provide hand-washing facilities and cleaning tools; garbage collection; and promote hygiene through training.

WASH committees will be established in the camps to oversee the management of the water points and the hygiene promotion activities</narrative>
  </description>
